    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Sensitivity C — Study-system (sys_id) random effect\"\n---\n\n\n\n## What this tests\n\nProtocol §3.7 (final analysis) and §3.5. Contrasts from the same study system\nmay be non-independent because they share a population, location, disturbance\nhistory, or research programme. The primary model captures study-level\ndependence through `ref_id` and shared ancestry through the phylogeny, but does\n**not** include a separate study-system term, because `sys_id`, `ref_id`, and\nspecies identity are strongly associated in PROCEED — most systems map to a\nsingle species and often a single source — so including all three risks poorly\nidentified variance components. This analysis adds `(1 | sys_id)` to each\nincluded moderator model and reports the outcome explicitly, per the protocol's\ncommitment to flag weak identifiability rather than interpret confounded\ncomponents separately. The full dataset is used.\n\n## How it was fit\n\nFit on `totoro`, not at render — 4 chains × 4,000 iterations (2,000 warmup),\n`adapt_delta = 0.97`, `max_treedepth = 15`, `cmdstanr`.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nphylo   <- prepare_phylo_and_data(dat_mod, A_full)\nformula <- build_ls_formula(moderator, has_phylogeny = phylo$has_phylo,\n                            has_sys_id = TRUE)              # + (1 | sys_id)\nfit     <- fit_ls_model(\n  phylo$dat_model, formula,\n  build_ls_priors(formula, phylo$dat_model, phylo$V, A = phylo$A_mod),\n  V = phylo$V, A = phylo$A_mod, mcmc_args = default_mcmc_args)\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Convergence diagnostics\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-condensed\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<caption>Convergence diagnostics (4 chains, 2000 post-warmup draws each).</caption>\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Moderator </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Max R̂ </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Min bulk ESS </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Min tail ESS </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Divergences </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:right;\"> Max-treedepth hits </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> Disturbance context (m01) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 1.0081 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 645 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 1329 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 21 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(248, 215, 218, 255) !important;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Comparison design (m02) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0075 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 699 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1459 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 7 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Environmental-change context (m08) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0069 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 630 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1133 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 2 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Elapsed time — log₁₀ generations (m04) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0048 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 610 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1009 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 2 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Phenotypic vs genetic study (m07) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0047 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 907 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1607 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Elapsed time — log₁₀ years (m03) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0045 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 823 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 915 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Trait type (m05) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1.0089 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 559 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 1028 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:right;\"> 0 </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {.callout-warning}\nThe **disturbance** model returned 21 divergent transitions and the **design**\nmodel 7. This is the weak-identifiability signal the protocol anticipated: with\n`sys_id` added on top of `ref_id` and the phylogeny, the sampler struggles in\npart of the posterior. R̂ (< 1.01) and ESS remain acceptable, but the individual\n`sys_id`, `ref_id`, and phylogenetic variance components should **not** be\ninterpreted separately for these models.\n:::\n\n## Reading the tables\n\nRaw location–scale coefficients on treatment coding: the **Intercept** row is the\nreference-level value, each other row the difference from it. The matched\n**primary** (no `sys_id`) coefficient is shown alongside, and the **Stability**\ncolumn reads *consistent* when the two share sign and the same 95%\ncredible-interval conclusion, **DIFFERS** (highlighted) otherwise. Stability of\nthe moderator coefficients here indicates the reported effects are not artefacts\nof omitting a study-system term.\n\n**Overall:**  7 of 36 moderator coefficients change their credible-interval conclusion relative to the primary fit. \n\n## Results by moderator\n\n\n### Disturbance context (m01)\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-condensed\" style=\"width: auto !important; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n<caption>Disturbance context (m01)</caption>\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sub-model </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Term </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Sensitivity β [95% CrI] </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Primary β [95% CrI] </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:left;\"> Stability </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;vertical-align: top !important;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\" rowspan=\"7\"> Location (mean lnM) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\"> Intercept (ref.) </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\"> -0.694 [-1.241, -0.094] </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\"> -0.495 [-1.281, 0.315] </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;font-weight: bold;background-color: rgba(255, 243, 205, 255) !important;\"> DIFFERS </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   \n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Hunt_harv </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> -0.034 [-0.497, 0.426] </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> -0.260 [-0.620, 0.089] </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> consistent </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   \n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> Introduction </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 0.182 [-0.288, 0.653] </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> 0.007 [-0.396, 0.396] </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> consistent </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   \n   <td style=\"text-align:left;\"> La